 "how": "a reading built on computed results, with no new computation: what passing from m000 to its double cover m004 keeps, loses and gains, row by row, and what follows for the even-tick condition under the note's stated identification (level n of the tower stands for a history of n ticks). Every figure in its table is settled at parts 1 and 2a and recomputed on main (the Klein-bottle cusp; twisted duality with the untwisted form failing at levels 3, 5, 7: web-wc8p2a-01; 12, 210 and 1,892 modules with index +-1 on 4 + 4, 36 + 36, 244 + 244: web-wf9-01; 48 and 2,420 doublets; class index 0 at odd levels; the characters' gaps 1, 4, 11, 29; the hand (-1)^(n+e): web-wc8p1-01). Its reading: the class index cannot see odd ticks at all, so it is no test of the condition; a test would have to run through an observable that does not vanish at odd ticks, and two were found, the characters' h^1 gaps and the hand at the mark",
 "note": "A LEAD for the ruling that even ticks are a condition the weight must deliver: the note names the two observables a derivation would have to use. Later cards carry it further (W-F4: the odd tick's classes are its double cover's; W-F19: the zero index at odd levels is a theorem).",
